<p><code>Pdf::extractTextFromFile()</code> and <code>::extractTextFromData()</code> pull the text layer back out of an
existing PDF. Extraction is native to Pop PDF — no external binary, no third-party PDF library —
and decodes text against embedded and CID fonts as well as the standard names; see
<a href="#embedded-and-cid-fonts">Embedded and CID Fonts</a>.</p>
<h2 id="extracting-from-a-file">Extracting From a File<a class="anchor" href="#extracting-from-a-file" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p><code>extractTextFromFile($file, $pages = null, $pageLimit = null, $password = null)</code> takes a path and
returns one string:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;

<span class="text-var">$text</span> = <span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">extractTextFromFile</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/report.pdf&#039;</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>Given a three-page <code>report.pdf</code>, one line of text on each page, that returns every page's text
joined into a single value:</p>
