a page with no text contributes.</p>
<p><code>$file</code> has to point at something on disk — a path that does not exist raises
<code>Pop\Pdf\Extract\Exception</code>:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Extract\Exception</span>;

<span class="text-kw">try</span> {
    <span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">extractTextFromFile</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/missing.pdf&#039;</span>);
} <span class="text-kw">catch</span> (<span class="text-type">Exception</span> <span class="text-var">$exception</span>) {
    <span class="text-kw">echo</span> <span class="text-var">$exception</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getMessage</span>();
}
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>That prints <code>Error: That PDF file does not exist.</code> A path that exists but isn't a valid PDF raises
the same exception with a different message — <code>extractTextFromFile()</code> on a plain text file, or
<code>extractTextFromData()</code> on a string that isn't PDF bytes at all, both fail with <code>Error: Could not resolve the PDF document catalog (Root).</code></p>
<h2 id="extracting-from-raw-bytes">Extracting From Raw Bytes<a class="anchor" href="#extracting-from-raw-bytes" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p><code>extractTextFromData($data, $pages = null, $pageLimit = null)</code> is the same call against a string of
PDF bytes instead of a path — for a document that was uploaded, fetched over HTTP, or generated in
memory and never written to disk:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;

<span class="text-var">$data</span> = <span class="text-fn">file_get_contents</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/report.pdf&#039;</span>);
<span class="text-var">$text</span> = <span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">extractTextFromData</span>(<span class="text-var">$data</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>Both methods load their input into the same <code>Extract\Document</code> and run the identical walk over it,
so the same file returns the identical string either way — which one to call is a question of what
you already have in hand, a path or a buffer.</p>
<h2 id="selecting-pages">Selecting Pages<a class="anchor" href="#selecting-pages" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p><code>$pages</code> is the third argument on both methods — an array of 1-based page numbers, or a single
number on its own; <code>2</code> and <code>[2]</code> mean the same thing:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;

<span class="text-var">$second</span>        = <span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">extractTextFromFile</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/report.pdf&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">pages</span>: <span class="text-num">2</span>);
<span class="text-var">$firstAndThird</span> = <span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">extractTextFromFile</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/report.pdf&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">pages</span>: [<span class="text-num">1</span>, <span class="text-num">3</span>]);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p><code>$second</code> is <code>&quot;Page Two text.&quot;</code>; <code>$firstAndThird</code> is <code>&quot;Page One text.\n\nPage Three text.&quot;</code>.</p>
<ul>
<li>selection follows <strong>document order, not list order</strong> — <code>pages: [3, 1]</code> returns page one's text
first, exactly what <code>pages: [1, 3]</code> returns</li>
<li>a page number past the end of the document drops out of the selection rather than raising —
<code>[1, 9]</code> on a three-page document returns page 1's text alone</li>
<li>a selection that matches nothing — every number out of range, or an empty array — returns <code>''</code>
rather than raising, the same string an empty page returns; counting the result against the
request is the only way to tell the two apart</li>
</ul>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;

<span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">extractTextFromFile</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/report.pdf&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">pages</span>: [<span class="text-num">9</span>]); <span class="text-comment">// &#039;&#039; — page 9 doesn&#039;t exist</span>
<span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">extractTextFromFile</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/report.pdf&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">pages</span>: []);  <span class="text-comment">// &#039;&#039; — nothing was asked for</span>
</code></pre>
</div>

<h2 id="limiting-how-much-is-walked">Limiting How Much Is Walked<a class="anchor" href="#limiting-how-much-is-walked" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p><code>$pageLimit</code> is the fourth argument, and caps extraction to the document's first <em>n</em> pages:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;

<span class="text-var">$firstTwo</span> = <span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">extractTextFromFile</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/report.pdf&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">pageLimit</span>: <span class="text-num">2</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>That returns <code>&quot;Page One text.\n\nPage Two text.&quot;</code>. A limit larger than the document, <code>99</code> on a
three-page file, returns every page, the same as no limit at all — and the limit is enforced during
the walk, not by truncating the joined string: pages beyond it are never decompressed or
interpreted, so a low limit on a long document skips real work, not only output.</p>
<p>An explicit <code>$pages</code> list wins outright over <code>$pageLimit</code>, which only applies when <code>$pages</code> is
<code>null</code>:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;

<span class="text-var">$text</span> = <span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">extractTextFromFile</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/report.pdf&#039;</span>, <span class="text-type">pages</span>: [<span class="text-num">3</span>], <span class="text-type">pageLimit</span>: <span class="text-num">1</span>);
<span class="text-comment">// &quot;Page Three text.&quot; — the explicit list, not the first page the limit would have picked</span>
</code></pre>
</div>

<h2 id="how-pages-are-separated">How Pages Are Separated<a class="anchor" href="#how-pages-are-separated" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p>Pages join with a blank line, <code>&quot;\n\n&quot;</code>, and only between pages that actually produced text — a page
with no text at all contributes nothing, not even an empty entry:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;

<span class="text-comment">// A three-page document where the middle page carries no text at all</span>
<span class="text-var">$text</span> = <span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">extractTextFromFile</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/mixed-report.pdf&#039;</span>);
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>That returns <code>&quot;First page has text.\n\nThird page has text.&quot;</code> — no trace of the blank page between
them. Selecting it on its own, <code>pages: 2</code>, returns <code>''</code>, the same as any other selection matching
nothing.</p>
<h2 id="embedded-and-cid-fonts">Embedded and CID Fonts<a class="anchor" href="#embedded-and-cid-fonts" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></h2>

<p>Extraction decodes text against whatever font drew it, including a font embedded in the document
itself, not only the standard names: an embedded TrueType or OpenType font decodes as two-byte
glyph IDs through its own character map, while a standard or embedded Type1 font stays on a
single-byte path. A compressed content stream — Flate, LZW, RunLength, ASCII85 or ASCIIHex, in any
combination a producer chose to apply — extracts the same as one left uncompressed.</p>
<p>The round trip is the way to see this working rather than take it on faith: write non-ASCII text
through an embedded TrueType font and extract it straight back.</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
<div class="code-window-bar"><span class="code-lang">PHP</span><button type="button" class="code-copy" @click="copy()" :aria-label="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy code'" aria-label="Copy code"><svg x-show="!copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11.5" height="11.5" rx="2.4"></rect><path d="M15 5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 12.4 3H5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 3 5.6v6.8A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 5.6 15"></path></svg><svg x-show="copied" x-cloak class="code-copied" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 12.5 9 17l10.5-10.5"></path></svg></button></div>
<pre><code><span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Page\Text</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Document\Font</span>;
<span class="text-kw">use</span> <span class="text-type">Pop\Pdf\Pdf</span>;

<span class="text-var">$font</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Font</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/fonts/DejaVuSans.ttf&#039;</span>);

<span class="text-var">$document</span> = <span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Document</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Page</span>(<span class="text-type">Page</span>::<span class="text-num">LETTER</span>));
<span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">embedFont</span>(<span class="text-var">$font</span>);

<span class="text-var">$original</span> = <span class="text-str">&#039;Café Müller — €120 naïve&#039;</span>;
<span class="text-var">$document</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getPage</span>(<span class="text-num">1</span>)-&gt;<span class="text-fn">addText</span>(<span class="text-kw">new</span> <span class="text-type">Text</span>(<span class="text-var">$original</span>, <span class="text-type">size</span>: <span class="text-num">24</span>), <span class="text-var">$font</span>-&gt;<span class="text-fn">getName</span>(), <span class="text-type">x</span>: <span class="text-num">72</span>, <span class="text-type">y</span>: <span class="text-num">700</span>);

<span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">writeToFile</span>(<span class="text-var">$document</span>, <span class="text-type">filename</span>: <span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/embedded.pdf&#039;</span>);

<span class="text-var">$extracted</span> = <span class="text-type">Pdf</span>::<span class="text-fn">extractTextFromFile</span>(<span class="text-kw">__DIR__</span> . <span class="text-str">&#039;/embedded.pdf&#039;</span>);

<span class="text-var">$extracted</span> <span class="text-kw">===</span> <span class="text-var">$original</span>; <span class="text-comment">// true</span>
</code></pre>
</div>

<p>The accented letter, umlaut, em dash and euro sign all survive, and the bytes match exactly, not
only the visible characters:</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
